# Codex Adversarial Review

Target: working tree diff
Verdict: needs-attention

No-ship. The v2 plan still has enforceability gaps around verified promotion, migration ordering, inventory completeness, and the new partial-verified status.

Findings:
- [high] Catalog raw-artifact gate is described but not enforceable by the migration manifest (plan.md:610-621)
  P2 requires source_id, raw_path, raw_sha256, captured_date, audit_status, and a ban on verified without raw artifacts, but the actual phase2a manifest schema omits source_id, raw_path, raw_sha256, and captured_date. A catalog note can therefore be marked citation_status_target=verified/audit_status=audited without the manifest preserving the artifact identity or hash needed to audit or rollback that decision.
  Recommendation: Make the phase2a manifest the single gate: include source_id, raw_path, raw_sha256, captured_date, and require citation_status_target=verified only when audit_status=audited, source_id/raw_path are nonempty, local raw_path exists, and local raw_sha256 matches.
- [high] Copy-verify-archive order validates before link rewrite and deletes before the final integrity check (plan.md:630-633)
  Step 2a.4 claims link rewrite validation, but the actual link rewrite is deferred to 2a.7 after archive and after the 2a.6 staging removal gate. This either makes 2a.4 impossible to pass repo-wide, or worse, lets validation scope exclude existing concept references and leaves broken _staging links after the source tree has been moved/deleted.
  Recommendation: Move link rewrite before validation, run a repo-wide grep for _staging references after rewrites, then archive. Do not remove _staging or treat the phase as passed until the repo-wide link check and validators pass after rewrites.
- [high] Canonical table still allows verified promotion before source verification (plan.md:651)
  storm-surge/05 is targeted as verified while the same row says the user still must directly confirm each KHOA Annual Report section/page. That leaves the original accidental-verified failure mode open: implementation can follow the target column and promote unconfirmed surge values into the objective layer.
  Recommendation: Set this target to source-needed until exact report/page evidence exists, or split it into per-report rows with source_id, page/section, raw artifact path/hash, and only promote rows whose evidence has already been checked.
- [medium] Manifest inventory counts are internally inconsistent, so files can be skipped (plan.md:576-627)
  The plan says P1 has 10 notes, but the listed failure-patterns/heuristics/playbooks items total 11. It then sizes the manifest as 10 + 35 = 45 notes. The working tree has 50 files under _staging/from-modeling-wiki/knowledge, so this manual count is already stale. A skipped file can be archived or later deleted without ever receiving classification, destination, or hash coverage.
  Recommendation: Generate the manifest from `find _staging/from-modeling-wiki/knowledge -type f`, add an explicit include/exclude decision for every file including READMEs, and gate 2a.1 on manifest source_path set equality with the discovered file set.
- [medium] partial-verified is planned before policy and validator compatibility is mandatory (plan.md:663-677)
  The plan assigns partial-verified targets in 2b, but CONVENTIONS currently only permits draft-unsourced/source-needed/verified and says citing any non-verified note downgrades the citing page to source-needed. The plan makes CONVENTIONS changes optional or deferred, and never adds a concrete validator/template update gate. That can create frontmatter states the repo policy does not recognize and unclear downstream citation semantics.
  Recommendation: Add a mandatory 2b.0 gate before any partial-verified document is created: update CONVENTIONS, templates, INDEX semantics, and any status validators/tests; define whether partial-verified counts as verified or source-needed for downstream citations.

Next steps:
- Fix the manifest schema and inventory gate first; they control data loss and verified promotion safety.
- Reorder 2a so link rewrite happens before validation/archive/delete.
- Resolve partial-verified policy before using it, or keep wrapper pages source-needed.
